Z||000007||Raydar||04-25-2000||10:03 AM||||Terryk. Of course, you're right. The "redesign" already existed, but the beancounters "beat it down". <BR>As for the differences between the early cars and the 88's, I've never really driven either at "the edge", as some of you have, but the 88 seems to be a bit easier to drive, especially on long trips.||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||04-25-2000||11:52 AM||||Raydar,<P>I think I see what you mean. The steering doesn't seem as busy on the 88's.||||reg||1
Z||000009||87GT||04-25-2000||07:17 PM||||I think my 87GT handles very well from 0-45 mph, but after that I do notice it gets a little more floaty and sometimes wants to do things on its own, but I have gotten use to it.  Im kinda picky on this sort of thing, so it may not seem like anything to other 84-87 owners.  Ive never driven an 88 fiero but I have heard reactions from, nothing different, to wow, big difference!  Ill have to find out for myself. :-) I do want a T-Top fiero really bad.  I always invision myself going down the highway with them out!||||reg||1
